course: dictionary
lesson: 2334
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and crumb is one of them. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning the writer means. «She brushed the crumbs off the table after lunch.» The table is after lunch, so crumbs must be tiny bits of food.
explain: The same word can also mean a very small amount of something. «There is not a crumb of hope left.» Hope is not a kind of food, so crumb must mean a tiny amount. Always ask: does my meaning fit the sentence? If you try "tiny bit of food" here, it makes no sense, so you know to look for another meaning.
explain: Crumbs! is different again. It is not about food at all. When Ella opens the door and sees her whole class waiting, she might shout «Crumbs!». It is an old-fashioned British way of showing surprise, a bit like "Goodness!" The exclamation mark and the feeling around it are your clues.
fact: A crumb is a very small piece of bread, cake or biscuit.
fact: A crumb can also be a very small amount of something, as in «a crumb of comfort».
fact: «Crumbs!» is an old-fashioned British way of showing surprise.
fact: Breadcrumbs are tiny pieces of bread used in cooking, for example to coat fish fingers.
fact: In the story of Hansel and Gretel, the children dropped a trail of crumbs.
exercise: «She brushed the crumbs off the table after lunch.» What are the crumbs? | Drops of water | Small stones from the garden | *Tiny pieces of food | Tiny pieces of paper
exercise: «There is not a crumb of hope left.» What does crumb mean here? | A loud noise | *A very small amount | A big piece of cake | A type of bird
exercise: Ella opens the door and sees her whole class waiting. She shouts «Crumbs!». What does this show? | Anger | Tiredness | *Surprise | Hunger
test: «That is why a tiny ant can carry a crumb many times its weight.» What is the crumb in this sentence? | A heavy stone | *A very small piece of food | A tiny ant | A large cake
test: Breadcrumbs are used to coat food like fish fingers. What are breadcrumbs? | Large slices of bread for toast | Bread that has gone mouldy | *Tiny bits of bread used in cooking | Tiny bits of wood used for fires
exam: Which meaning fits «a crumb of comfort» best? | *A very small amount of comfort | A kind of food | A large pile of comfort | A loud, surprised shout
